    "body": "I'm having the same issue on a fresh Pop!_OS install. I don't have ```grml-zsh-config``` installed, and am using the default ```.zshrc``` for now.\r\n\r\nRunning ```eval \"$(starship init zsh)\"``` while in the ```zsh``` prompt also appears to do nothing.\r\n\r\n```\r\n~ % starship --version\r\nstarship 0.51.0\r\ntag:v0.51.0\r\ncommit_hash:\r\nbuild_time:2021-03-23 16:36:25\r\nbuild_env:rustc 1.50.0 (cb75ad5db 2021-02-10),\r\n```\r\n```\r\nzsh --version\r\nzsh 5.8 (x86_64-ubuntu-linux-gnu)\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt's not exactly clear to me how you would go about downgrading to v0.50.0 with the current curl install method.",
